  "name": "Cantes mineros (taranta, minera, cartagenera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The cantes mineros, or cantes de Levante, are the free-rhythm, fandango-derived flamenco songs of the mining districts of eastern Andalusia and Murcia: the taranta of Almería and Linares, the minera and cartagenera of La Unión and Cartagena, and the levantica and murciana. Antonio Chacón shaped several of them for the professional stage, and since 1961 the Festival Internacional del Cante de las Minas in La Unión has made them a competition repertoire; the metred taranto is their danceable offshoot.",
  "recipe": "classic Iberian early-1960s cantes mineros, ballad Poetry, Mediterranean ballad branch. cante jondo, solo with instrumental accompaniment, flamenco quejio ayeo temple afilla quiebro tercio, single lead single track no stacking. cypress body percussive attack strong flamenco tradition rasgueado strum picado scale runs flamenco guitar. andalusian tablao seville madrid. Neumann U47, tube pre, colored vintage console, LA-2A optical, passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
